    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0338v3</id>
    <title>Geometric quantization of integrable systems with hyperbolic singularities</title>
    <updated>2009-02-04T11:41:15Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0338v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0808.0338v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We construct the geometric quantization of a compact surface using a singular real polarization coming from an integrable system. Such a polarization always has singularities, which we assume to be of nondegenerate type. In particular, we compute the effect of hyperbolic singularities, which make an infinite-dimensional contribution to the quantization, thus showing that this quantization depends strongly on polarization.</summary>
    <category term="math.SG" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math-ph" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2008-08-03T18:42:56Z</published>
